movie magic is what transports us to  unique worlds  and what brings magical characters to  life but have you ever wondered what  some  iconic screen moments would look like  without their visual effects  in this video we'll be taking you behind  the scenes of some of the most iconic  moments from your favorite movies and tv  shows  as much as we wish it was possible we  all know that humans  just can't fly and that the hulk just  doesn't exist  so how exactly do they make things like  superheroes and dinosaurs seem so real  it all happens in the editing room so  let's take a look at the behind the  scenes  of sets like maleficent the hunger games  and the avengers before all the cgi gets  added in  would you like to see is it safe from  the monstrous waves to the debris that  line the water during battle  pirates of the caribbean is full of  dashes of cgi and vfx editing that bring  the movie to life  but there's one specific moment from the  dead men tell no tales  that looks completely different behind  the scenes  the ghost shark scene featuring jack  sparrow and henry turner was filmed in  three different locations  an actual outdoor scenery a small water  tank  and an indoor set that was completely  blue screen  their rowboat was put on a gimbal so  that it would give the appearance that  they were  actually being attacked by sharks  angelina jolie put her all into the  making of maleficent but no matter how  much of a renegade she was on screen  her character would not have come to  life without the help of cgi  vfx and a very interesting machine  called a fork tuner  angelina was secured into a machine that  was controlled by other people  in order to get the motions right they  basically became puppets while filming  everything was completely blue screen  and her wings were added later on in  editing  the fairies in their small form were  also completely animated using a special  program  the actress's faces were processed so  that they'd be able to copy their exact  animation later on  it's probably no surprise that the  majority of this film is cgi and visual  effects  but what might surprise you is how baby  groot and rocket looked behind the  scenes  they were well basically not there both  characters are completely cgi  [Music]  during filming they'd have stuffed  animals and models as stand-ins so the  actors wouldn't be completely lost  beauty and the beast is where most  millennials got their first taste of  love  and romance but there's nothing lovely  and romantic about how beauty and the  beast looked behind the scenes  dan stevens didn't have a super  realistic beast costume  instead he wore a motion capture suit  the costume helped the editors use cgi  to make the beast come to life later on  the br guest scene was also  pretty lackluster behind the scenes  lumiere's grand performance was later  added in during  editing which left emma watson acting at  a fancy table alone  be our guest  avatar took 10 years to make so you can  only imagine  how much effort went into making  everything perfect  pandora itself was created completely  using green screen and vfx  but what's even more interesting is the  way the avatars were brought to life  the actors wore motion capture suits to  film their scenes and also had to get 3d  models of themselves done  so they could digitally make their  avatar based on their appearance later  on  looks like you this is your avatar now  jake  a whopping 300 shots were made using vfx  for divergent to produce the utopian  city we see in the film  that includes the dauntless train  jumping scene that catapults tris  into the world of danger it was actually  filmed in six different locations  with a platform that was completely made  later with visual effects  what you see in the film is actually the  editing team blending clips from  different locations to seamlessly fit  together  is it just me or are they trying to kill  us  taylor lautner didn't get a special wolf  suit instead he explored the magical  qualities grey spandex had to offer  and acted out his scenes with kristen  stewart to make sure she got the eye  contact right  then the vfx team did their magic and  created jacob's wolf form later on  they also used cgi to edit actress  mackenzie foy's face  on different age children after renesmee  was born  let's just be grateful we dodged them  using chuck esme  it was nessie who wanted me there nessie  you nicknamed my daughter after the walk  this monster  grey's anatomy may not have the need for  fancy editing like cgi and vfx  but their special effects and prop team  have their work cut out for them  the show brings to life some pretty  realistic medical procedures what you're  actually seeing is the actors working on  a dummy  full of animal intestines what the hell  is that thing oh that is a kidney in a  jar that's not a bear how did you get  that  in narnia characters like aslan were  completely computer generated  the actors would have to act out their  scenes alone to make it a little bit  easier they would have stand-ins where  the character would be  for aslin they even came up with a type  of model that could be controlled by  someone inside  that way they could get some of his  movements naturally  girl on fire catching fire fire was a  huge part of the hunger games franchise  and the majority of the time  it was added into shots using cgi and  vfx  well i was just hoping that i wouldn't  burn to death  for instance katniss's costumes both in  the first second  and third films were all thanks to the  editing team  and jennifer lawrence actually filmed  the scene where katniss runs from the  flames in the arena  completely without fire the dark forest  was huge in the wizard of oz spin-off  and it wouldn't have been able to come  alive without cgi  hate the dark forest hate the dark  forest during filming james franco  actually had to dodge poles meant to be  the tree branches  of the forest that were controlled by  the crew the china glass girl was also  completely done in the editing room for  the space scenery in the movie  almost everything was shot using a green  screen the filmmakers also had to find  the perfect way to make it seem like the  actors were acting without gravity  for the majority of the filming they  were strapped into a harness to give the  camera effect that they were floating in  space  the red queen might not have seemed as  malicious and intimidating if it wasn't  for her disproportioned head  or if it wasn't helena bonham carter i  used to have the white queen  now her head is so small tiny it's  purple of a head  but her body proportions were only  altered in editing  for filming she looked completely normal  there were also a bunch of other iconic  scenes that looked interesting behind  the scenes  welcome to jurassic world jurassic world  may have had its audiences believing  that dinosaurs might one day roam the  earth again  but for a lot of the filming no type of  dinosaur  fake or real was even present instead  the actors would perform the scene while  being mindful of the markers that told  them where the dinosaurs were meant to  be  if the actor had a scene where they were  interacting with the dinosaur  they would have people dress up in fake  dinosaur heads and act as a stand-in  the most impressive part of the avengers  end game is probably how well they made  the hulk scenes come to life  mark ruffalo wore a special motion suit  and headpiece while acting  so that they'd later be able to  transform him and his facial features  into the hero put the brains and the bra  together  and now look at me best of both worlds  another notable cgi moment is when they  had to actually use programs to create  captain marvel's hair  the iconic moment that black panther  rose from the fire and ashes  to show everyone he was still alive i am  not dead  is probably something i and a lot of  other marvel fans  will never forget but behind the scenes  all chadwick boseman had to do  was step onto some foam blocks and the  rest was  all edited in the only character in the  jungle book who wasn't the product of  cgi  or vfx was mowgli the rest of his jungle  friends were made with cgi  the actor had fake animals on set to  help him imagine the scene  and deliver his lines better the  majority of the jungle was  also completely done using cgi  relax kid no need to get worked up okay  daenerys flying her dragon is nothing  short of magical  but behind the scenes it was a little  less  graceful they had amelia clark climb up  on an animatronic dragon  surrounded by a green screen that would  mimic the movements of flying  the editor's job was to bring all of  that to life  sorry to say folks but gollum really  doesn't exist  not even behind the scenes unless you  count his actor  andy circus dressed up in a motion suit  saying  but the credit all goes to the visual  effects team who brought the character  to life  perfectly are we really surprised that a  portion of this film was spent on a  yacht  all these scenes were actually filmed in  a studio with green screens  the iconic scene where the yacht is  taken over by some pretty intense waves  wouldn't have been possible without cgi  and visual effects either  [Music]  some of these scenarios look nothing  like the final product we saw on screen  it makes you realize that acting is a  lot more than just  reading off of a script and that a  film's editing and special effects team  deserves way more credit than they get  what behind the scenes moment was the  most shocking for you don't forget to  hit that subscribe button  and give this video a huge thumbs up for  movie magic  [Music]  you
 

